WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:07.831
It was early morning, and two workers at Shopwell Supermarket were stocking shelves.

2
00:00:07.832 --> 00:00:13.114
"We have too many canned tomatoes, Meg," one worker said, looking in boxes.

3
00:00:13.115 --> 00:00:16.794
"They won't fit on the shelf."

4
00:00:16.795 --> 00:00:20.661
"Let's stack them near the cash registers," Meg said.

5
00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:24.988
"We need to hurry—the store opens soon."

6
00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:29.942
As they carried the boxes down an aisle, Meg spotted some empty shelves.

7
00:00:29.943 --> 00:00:33.932
"We stocked those shelves earlier. Where did all the food go?"

8
00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:37.632
Something crunched under Daryl's foot, and he looked down.

9
00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:41.198
Crumbs and wrappers were scattered across the floor.

10
00:00:41.199 --> 00:00:45.726
"Have you been eating stuff, Daryl?" Meg asked, putting down her box.

11
00:00:45.727 --> 00:00:49.220
"Of course not!" Daryl replied.

12
00:00:49.221 --> 00:00:50.656
"Then who's been eating?"

13
00:00:50.657 --> 00:00:52.612
Snort!

14
00:00:52.613 --> 00:00:56.160
Startled, Daryl dropped his boxes.

15
00:00:56.161 --> 00:00:58.156
"What was that noise?"

16
00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:03.927
Meg gestured toward the end of the aisle, and they tiptoed toward the sound.

17
00:01:03.928 --> 00:01:07.814
Snort! Suddenly a large figure leaped out.

18
00:01:07.815 --> 00:01:16.071
"Ahh!" Meg and Daryl ran.

19
00:01:16.072 --> 00:01:20.890
*** "Jack, what are you doing?" Miss Apricot asked with a

20
00:01:20.891 --> 00:01:26.607
frown. Jack was crawling on the floor. "My pencil rolled off my

21
00:01:26.608 --> 00:01:30.818
desk." Roxy reached down. "Here it

22
00:01:30.819 --> 00:01:34.585
is." The teacher folded her arms and gave Jack a stern

23
00:01:34.586 --> 00:01:44.146
look. "You're supposed to be reading quietly—not searching for your

24
00:01:44.147 --> 00:01:47.380
pencil." Jack sat down and spun his pencil

25
00:01:47.381 --> 00:01:52.333
around. "My book is boring. I wish it was time for

26
00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:55.689
recess." "I'm enjoying my book," Terrell

27
00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:58.654
said. "It's about the Silk

28
00:01:58.655 --> 00:02:00.819
Road." Mara

29
00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:06.104
groaned. "Is your book boring too?" Roxy

30
00:02:06.105 --> 00:02:10.882
asked. "I like my book, but I'm so hungry," Mara

31
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:16.166
said. "I can't wait for lunch—it's Pizza Day," Terrell

32
00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:20.869
said. "Mmm, I can smell it cooking," Mara said.

33
00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:24.332
Jack sniffed. "Me too!"

34
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:27.570
Miss Apricot frowned. "Shh!"

35
00:02:27.571 --> 00:02:31.556
Jack grinned sheepishly. "Sorry!"

36
00:02:31.557 --> 00:02:34.539
Roxy's watch beeped.

37
00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.798
"I'll be right back, Miss Apricot.

38
00:02:36.799 --> 00:02:41.888
I need to, um, use the restroom."

39
00:02:41.889 --> 00:02:45.281
Roxy ran into the hallway and opened her watch.

40
00:02:45.282 --> 00:02:48.051
"Mayor Bloom. What's wrong?"

41
00:02:48.052 --> 00:02:54.320
"Rocket Girl," Mayor Bloom said, "there's a food thief in Metro City."

42
00:02:54.321 --> 00:02:57.315
"A food thief?" Roxy repeated.

43
00:02:57.316 --> 00:03:02.896
Mayor Bloom nodded. "The thief is eating food without paying for it."

44
00:03:02.897 --> 00:03:04.484
"I'll check it out, Mayor.

45
00:03:04.485 --> 00:03:10.308
But I usually fight dangerous villains—not somebody who ate a meal and didn't pay."

46
00:03:10.309 --> 00:03:13.720
"The thief didn't just eat a meal," Mayor Bloom said.

47
00:03:13.721 --> 00:03:17.407
"He ate all the food at Shopwell Supermarket!"

48
00:03:17.408 --> 00:03:20.077
"Whoa!" Roxy gasped.

49
00:03:20.078 --> 00:03:24.723
"Then he ate all the food in two other food stores and several restaurants."

50
00:03:24.724 --> 00:03:29.869
Mayor Bloom shook his head. "He's in Metro City Bakery now."

51
00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:33.870
"The thief sounds like some sort of super eater," Roxy said.

52
00:03:33.871 --> 00:03:41.879
"Don't worry, Mayor—I'm on my way!"

53
00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.685
When Roxy arrived, police officers had surrounded Metro City Bakery.

54
00:03:46.686 --> 00:03:50.616
Detective Smith was watching from behind a police car.

55
00:03:50.617 --> 00:03:53.195
Roxy floated next to him.

56
00:03:53.196 --> 00:03:58.136
"Hi, Detective—I heard you have a big appetite today."

57
00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:02.321
"Very funny, Rocket Girl," Detective Smith said.

58
00:04:02.322 --> 00:04:05.376
"I didn't eat all the food."

59
00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:08.156
"Well, who did?" Roxy asked.

60
00:04:08.157 --> 00:04:11.267
"Do you have any information about the thief?"

61
00:04:11.268 --> 00:04:13.652
Detective Smith glanced at his notebook.

62
00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:18.598
"I interviewed two workers at Shopwell Supermarket who said the thief is a large—"

63
00:04:18.599 --> 00:04:22.645
Crash! The front of the bakery exploded.

64
00:04:22.646 --> 00:04:28.393
As the dust settled, a large figure stepped out and Roxy gasped.

65
00:04:28.394 --> 00:04:34.415
"A large pig!"

